"notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Newest usable poll is 62 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Russ Fulcher (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Idaho's 1st District is a heavily Republican seat, and incumbent Russ Fulcher is seeking another term after easily winning renomination. His Democratic challenger, Kaylee Peterson, has raised modest funds and trails badly in money, while independent Sarah Zabel has also attracted some support and attention. July polls showed Fulcher leading by roughly 10 to 21 points depending on how the independent candidate is treated, and prediction markets give Peterson only a small chance of winning.\n\nThe race has drawn little outside spending or national attention, and no expert raters list it as competitive. The main storyline has been Zabel's candidacy and a separate candidate's legal trouble, neither of which appears to threaten Fulcher's hold. The district's strong partisan lean and the incumbent's advantages make this a safe Republican seat, with the main uncertainty being the final margin rather than the winner.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0149, "margin": -16.84}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0123, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0169, "margin": -17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0127, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0192, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.006, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0083, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0149, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0221, "margin": -17.5}]}